{"author":{"id":"89da5fec8eff6d69dbcdd68f81be7e9163b16f34b17e978ecf3554487379f453"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1774044566,"nonce":"YWUimxQDVfx0Q+bM9YHC+KTEIvw=","title":"External CLI as first-class tier — channel-connected sessions as distribution model","message":"The MCP channel server (73e0adf) enables a distribution model where external Claude CLI sessions are first-class citizens:\n\n1. User installs Mandible (local daemon)\n2. User has Claude Code with their own claude.ai login\n3. User runs: claude --channels server:mandible\n4. Full Mandible integration — inbox, auth, work units, notifications\n\nThis makes external CLI the PRIMARY end-user distribution path:\n- No API keys needed (user's own Claude Code handles auth)\n- No OAuth concerns (Mandible is infrastructure, not an auth mediator)\n- ToS-compliant (user uses their own official Claude Code installation)\n- Users get full Mandible features just by adding a channel config\n\nThis elevates Tier 3 (external) from \"best-effort discovery\" to \"channel-connected first-class\" — potentially the most important tier for public distribution, even though SDK remains the most powerful for Mandible's own orchestration.\n\n## Implications\n- Session discovery should detect channel-connected sessions and treat them as high-fidelity\n- The Console tab should support viewing/interacting with channel-connected external sessions\n- Documentation should frame channel-connected as the recommended setup for end users\n- The work-unit model should support assignment to channel-connected sessions\n\nDepends on: 73e0adf (channel server), f3dbb3e (work-unit model)\nBlocked by: channels exiting research preview","files":null}]}